@startuml SD-XXX
' ============================================================
' Traceability: PREFIX-REQ-XXX | PREFIX-UC-XXX | PREFIX-RB-XXX
' PREFIX-UC-XXX: <Use Case Title>
' Stack: <fill in from iconix.config.yaml — language, framework, test framework>
'
' Each numbered group below corresponds to a UC step from PREFIX-UC-XXX.
' Each message becomes a method on a class in PREFIX-CLS-* (see note at bottom).
'
' Lifeline naming convention (v0.9.19+):
'   - Use stack-anchored, multi-line labels (\n) for boundaries and entities:
'       boundary "Razor View\nViews/Books/Detail.cshtml"
'       entity   "Book\n(EF Core entity)"
'   - Boundaries can carry stereotypes for UI dependencies (page reuse from
'     another UC):
'       boundary "Razor View\nViews/Shared/NotFound.cshtml" as BNFView <<from PREFIX-UC-XXX Show Book Details>>
'   - Use concrete actor names from the UC; never generic "User".
'
' SD-rendering rules (v0.9.19) — see agents/iconix-developer.md:
'   - Invoked UCs render as a synthetic boundary lifeline + explanatory note.
'   - UI dependencies render with `<<from PREFIX-UC-XXX Title>>` stereotype.
'   - Downstream consumers render as a lifeline at the right edge with a
'     dashed `..>` message from the producing entity.
'   - Framework helpers (e.g., MVC ModelBinder) render only when non-trivial.
' ============================================================

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #444444

' ── Lifelines: actor + boundaries + control + entities + DI interfaces ──

' Actor (concrete name from the UC; never generic "User"):
actor    "Customer (browser)"                      as Cust

' Boundaries (named pages, API surfaces; multi-line label allowed via \n):
boundary "Razor View\nViews/Books/Detail.cshtml"   as BDView
boundary "Razor View\nViews/Reviews/Write.cshtml"  as WRView

' UI dependency from another UC (stereotype shows reuse):
boundary "Razor View\nViews/Shared/NotFound.cshtml" as BNFView <<from PREFIX-UC-XXX Other-UC-Title>>

' Synthetic boundary for an invoked UC (when invocation surfaces a redirect):
boundary "Login redirect\n(cookie auth challenge)" as LoginRedir

' Framework controller lifeline (orchestrator) — named per stack convention:
control  "WriteCustomerReview\nController"        as Ctrl

' Framework-helper lifeline (only when non-trivial — e.g., it invokes
' IValidatableObject):
control  "ASP.NET Core\nModelBinder + ModelState" as MVC

' Application-layer DI interface (per Developer rule 4 — justify in
' class-model annotation or cdr-report):
control  "ICurrentUserService"                    as CurUser

' Domain entities (came from domain-model.puml, refined at M2):
entity   "CustomerSession"                        as CS
entity   "Book\n(EF Core entity)"                 as Book
entity   "CustomerReview\n: IValidatableObject"   as CR

' Repository pattern (visible per Developer rule 8):
entity   "IBookRepository\n(EfBookRepository)"    as BookRepo

' Downstream consumer (lifeline at right edge; dashed message from producer):
actor    "Moderator"                              as Mod

' ── Step 1 — UC step 1 — basic course ──
group Step 1 — <Customer action; system response> (RB controllers: CheckLogin, LoadBook)
  Cust    -> BDView : GET /resource
  BDView  -> Ctrl   : RouteAction()
  Ctrl    -> CurUser : GetSession(httpContext)
  CurUser -> CS     : new(claims)
  CS      --> CurUser : session
  CurUser --> Ctrl  : session
  Ctrl    -> CS     : IsLoggedIn
  CS      --> Ctrl  : true
  Ctrl    -> BookRepo : GetByIdAsync(id)
  BookRepo -> Book  : query
  Book    --> BookRepo : entity
  BookRepo --> Ctrl : Book (non-null)
end

' ── Step 2 — system response ──
group Step 2 — <System response> (RB controller: DisplayWriteReviewPage)
  Ctrl   --> WRView : View("Write", review)
  WRView --> Cust   : 200 OK
end

' ── Alternate Course A — invoked UC pattern ──
group Alternate A — <e.g., not logged in> #Pink
  Cust    -> BDView : GET /resource
  BDView  -> Ctrl   : RouteAction()
  Ctrl    -> CS     : IsLoggedIn
  CS      --> Ctrl  : false
  Ctrl    --> LoginRedir : Challenge() — 302 to /login
  LoginRedir --> Cust    : 302 redirect
  note right of Ctrl
    With [Authorize] on the action, the cookie-auth handler
    issues the 302 automatically. On successful login, Step 1
    re-executes. (Invoked UC: PREFIX-UC-XXX Login.)
  end note
end

' ── Alternate Course B — UI dependency pattern (Book Not Found page) ──
group Alternate B — <e.g., Book ID does not exist> #Pink
  Cust    -> BDView : GET /resource with unknown id
  BDView  -> Ctrl   : RouteAction()
  Ctrl    -> BookRepo : GetByIdAsync(id)
  BookRepo --> Ctrl : null
  Ctrl    --> BNFView : View("NotFound") — 404
  BNFView --> Cust    : 404
end

' ── Step N — downstream consumer pattern (queue handoff) ──
group Step N — <Save and enqueue>
  Ctrl   -> CR     : new(book, customer, text, rating)
  Ctrl   -> BookRepo : (persist via repository)
  CR     ..> Mod   : (downstream — read by PREFIX-UC-XXX Moderate; async)
end

note over Cust, Mod
  Class model derived from this diagram (PREFIX-CLS-*):
    PREFIX-CLS-WriteCustomerReviewController <<controller>>
       - WriteAsync(bookId)
       - SubmitAsync(review)
    PREFIX-CLS-CustomerReview <<entity>>
       - DataAnnotations + Validate(ValidationContext)
    PREFIX-CLS-ICurrentUserService <<service>>
       - GetSession(HttpContext) : CustomerSession

  Code skeleton paths (per architecture-package-map.md):
    src/Bookstore.Web/Controllers/WriteCustomerReviewController.cs
    src/Bookstore.Domain/CustomerReview.cs
    src/Bookstore.Application/ICurrentUserService.cs
    src/Bookstore.Infrastructure/Repositories/EfBookRepository.cs

  Traceability:
    PREFIX-REQ-XXX -> PREFIX-UC-XXX -> PREFIX-RB-XXX -> PREFIX-SD-XXX (this) -> CLS-* -> PREFIX-TC-*
end note

@enduml
